title: XXXX Local Government Collapses!
subtitle: The <span style="color: var(--rpp);"><strong>RPP</strong></span>'s first move against us...
view-if: year = 1928 and month = 5 and prarr_leader = "Facra"
max-visits: 1
tags: event
new-page: true

= XXXX Left-Wing Coalition Dissolved

Since the June 9365 election, the province of XXXX has been governed by a radical left coalition consisting of the <span style="color: var(--rpls);"><strong>RPL&S</strong></span>, <span style="color: var(--vp);"><strong>VPs</strong></span> and <span style="color: var(--prarr);"><strong>PRARR</strong></span>, with external support from the <span style="color: var(--pac);"><strong>PAC</strong></span>. It has been dubbed a bastion of the alt-left in the midst of an increasingly right-wing political landscape.

With the <span style="color: var(--prarr);"><strong>PRARR</strong></span> (now the <span style="color: var(--rpp);"><strong>RPP</strong></span>) having undergone a significant shift to the right, it was clear that the coalition's days were numbered. The <span style="color: var(--rpp);"><strong>RPP</strong></span> has now called a no-confidence motion to bring down our local government.

Some within our party have proposed forming a traffic light coalition by bringing the <span style="color: var(--adp);"><strong>ADP</strong></span> on board, which should be possible as long as we have maintained good enough relations with them.

- @adp_join: The <span style="color: var(--adp);"><strong>ADP</strong></span> will join our coalition!
- @adp_tolerate: Could we get the <span style="color: var(--adp);"><strong>ADP</strong></span> to abstain?
- @collapse: New elections will be called.

@adp_join
unavailable-subtitle: [? if ddp_relation < 50 : The <span style="color: var(--adp);"><strong>ADP</strong></span> does not trust us enough. ?] [? if kpd_relation < 30 : The <span style="color: var(--pac);"><strong>PAC</strong></span> may break toleration if this coalition were to be formed. ?] [? if resources < 2 : We do not have enough resources (2 needed). ?]
subtitle: -2 resources
choose-if: ddp_relation >= 50 and kpd_relation >= 30 and resources >= 2
on-arrival: resources -= 2; reformist_strength += 5; new_middle_spd += 3; workers_prarr += 3; ddp_relation += 5; rpls_relation += 3; kpd_relation -= 2;

We have managed to include the <span style="color: var(--adp);"><strong>ADP</strong></span> in our coalition!

@adp_tolerate
unavailable-subtitle: [? if ddp_relation < 50 : Our relations are not good enough. ?] [? if resources < 2 : We do not have enough resources (2 needed). ?]
subtitle: -2 resources
choose-if: ddp_relation >= 50 and resources >= 2
on-arrival: resources -= 2; reformist_strength += 5; new_middle_spd += 3; old_middle_prarr -= 2; rpls_relation += 3;

We have convinced the <span style="color: var(--adp);"><strong>ADP</strong></span> to abstain, thus making them de facto tolerators of the coalition.

@collapse
on-arrival: prarr_relation -= 5; old_middle_prarr += 5;

The coalition is no more more.
